powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "source": "{% comment %}
  Checklist Items (project owner, 2026-09-19).

  The items the paraplanner ticked inside the Intelligent Office task - Tax Check, High
  Risk Item 1, Enhanced Supervision and so on - which is WHY the case is being checked at
  all. The case has carried them since the extract was imported and nothing displayed
  them, so a checker opened a case with no way of knowing what had put it in front of
  them.

  NOT the checklist version's questions. Those are the check itself and the review form
  renders them directly; listing them here said the same thing twice.

  Read-only. al_checklistitems is written by the import and is the only input to the
  BR-004 route (ImportRules.ReadChecklist), so it records what the paraplanner selected
  rather than anything a checker may revise. Only the ticked items are stored - the case
  does not carry the vocabulary they were selected from - so there is no unticked row to
  draw, and a case naming none draws no heading either.

  Shared rather than copied (project owner, 2026-09-19): the review page showed this
  first and the case page shows it too, and the parsing below is the part that would
  drift. Usage:

    include 'OT Checklist Items' items: some.al_checklistitems variant: 'card'

  Parameters:
    items    the raw column value, newline separated.
    variant  'card' wraps the list in a standalone card, as the review page draws it
             around the form. Anything else - the case record page passes 'sheet' - is a
             plain section that takes the styling of whatever contains it.

  A bulleted list in both (project owner, 2026-09-19). The case page first drew a ruled
  table on the reasoning that .ot-checklist rules everything and a flowing list inside it
  reads as a foreign element; the owner asked for bullets there too, so the list is now
  the single shape and only the wrapper differs.

  The line break is turned into a single character before the split: this Liquid rejects
  a multi-character split, and newline_to_br writes a tag it understands whatever line
  endings the column happens to store.
{% endcomment %}

{% if items and items != '' %}
  {% assign ot_cl_flat = items | newline_to_br | replace: '<br />', '|' | replace: '<br>', '|' %}
  {% assign ot_cl_lines = ot_cl_flat | split: '|' %}

  {% comment %}
    Counted before anything is drawn. A case whose column holds only blank lines opens no
    section, rather than a heading over an empty list.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign ot_cl_count = 0 %}
  {% for l in ot_cl_lines %}
    {% assign ot_cl_item = l | strip %}
    {% if ot_cl_item != '' %}{% assign ot_cl_count = ot_cl_count | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}

  {% if ot_cl_count > 0 %}
    {% assign ot_cl_wrap = 'ot-checklist-overview' %}
    {% assign ot_cl_head = 'ot-checklist-overview__heading' %}
    {% if variant == 'card' %}
      {% assign ot_cl_wrap = 'ot-card ot-checklist-overview' %}
      {% assign ot_cl_head = 'ot-card__title' %}
    {% endif %}

    <section class="{{ ot_cl_wrap }}" aria-labelledby="ot-checklist-overview-heading">
      <h2 class="{{ ot_cl_head }}" id="ot-checklist-overview-heading">Checklist Items</h2>
      <ul class="ot-checklist-overview-items">
        {% for l in ot_cl_lines %}
          {% assign ot_cl_item = l | strip %}
          {% if ot_cl_item != '' %}
          <li>{{ ot_cl_item | escape }}</li>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
"
}
